{
  "kind": "safety-selection data config",
  "name": "study-v3-data-inj05",
  "purpose": "Headroom v2 (amendment draft 2026-10-05, user decisions D1-D2): the prepared data of study-v2-data-expanded-arc (prepared-v2) unchanged, plus 5% (507 rows) harmful PKU-SafeRLHF responses injected into the editable pool (prepare.INJECTION_RULE; nested: the 5% rows are the first rows of the 10% order) and the harm and over-refusal prompt banks split into development, selector and hidden parts at preparation (prepare.EVAL_BANK_RULE). Prepared before any v3 outcome exists. Licences: PKU-SafeRLHF CC BY-NC 4.0; HarmBench and StrongREJECT MIT; SimpleSafetyTests CC BY 2.0; OR-Bench and XSTest CC BY 4.0.",
  "amendments": [
    "2026-10-02, before any expanded outcome: the first preset asserted 302 toxicity-labelled ToxicChat prompts (4721 non-toxic, from an overlap-only metadata inspection that omitted within-test duplicate prompts). Strict preparation under these engine rules, with the pinned sources unchanged, excludes 60 prompts equal to an original DATE-LM prompt and drops 7 toxicity-labelled and 124 non-toxic within-test duplicate prompts, leaving 295 and 4597. Both counts are now asserted and the safety banks are 72 development / 80 selector / 143 hidden (hidden was 150); no bank shrinks at run time.",
    "2026-10-02: ARC-Easy eligible counts are now asserted: 570 validation and 2371 test (5 test questions duplicate an earlier question; no other exclusion). DATE-LM remains 83/66/9999 eligible training rows and 30 reference rows.",
    "2026-10-02: ARC overlap and disjointness checks compare the normalized bare question AND both rendered model inputs (generation and forced choice) with every original DATE-LM and ToxicChat prompt and with every emitted prompt. A source-only audit found no rendered collision with DATE-LM prompts in the pinned sources; the asserted counts refuse preparation if any appears.",
    "2026-10-02: the development seed namespace widens from 1101-1104 (an accidental four-seed execution restriction) to 1101-2099. Namespaces state allowed seeds, not planned or calibrated counts; selector 2101-8999 and reference 9101-9999 are unchanged and all three stay disjoint.",
    "design_seed 20261002 is the intentional preset construction seed, fixed before any outcome. The lead's engineering preparation check used a temporary seed and name; no seed is chosen in response to outcomes.",
    "2026-10-02 ~16:24UTC: replace initial ARC64generation/128MC banks with dev96generation+189MC, selector96generation+189MC, hidden256generation+2115MC. This uses every eligible ARC item once, improves rare-refusal resolution and substantially expands heldout capability coverage. Allocation is an engineering coverage compromise, not an optimized power guarantee. Old preparation/trajectories remain calibration-only and are never relabeled or resumed under the new manifest. No hidden outcomes or attribution advantage were inspected. No corpus, group, query, safety-bank or model changes.",
    "2026-10-05, headroom v2: extra_sources, injection and eval_banks added (pinned in sources/v2/sources-manifest.json); every earlier field is unchanged, so rows, ids, groups and the earlier banks equal prepared-v2's. HarmBench keeps 'standard' rows with an empty ContextString (contextual and copyright rows excluded); XSTest keeps prompts labelled safe (the contrast prompts are labelled unsafe).",
    "2026-10-05, headroom v2: the asserted counts (injection candidates 67020 and eligible 20348; harm bank 1267 and over-refusal bank 1569 eligible prompts) are those of the first preparation under these rules, recorded before any v3 outcome; preparation now refuses any difference.",
    "2026-10-05, headroom v2, lead's review of the first preparation, before any v3 outcome: (1) the over-refusal bank is split by source with fixed quotas (development 50 XSTest-safe + 50 OR-Bench hard, selector the same, hidden the rest; EVAL_BANK_RULE v2), because the proportional split left 10 XSTest prompts in development; (2) the injection walk skips a candidate whose prompt has character 5-gram Jaccard >= 0.5 with any evaluation prompt (NEAR_DUPLICATE), with an auditor-only report. The harm split and the asserted counts are unchanged."
  ],
